About Bostik, the adhesive solutions segment of Arkema Bostik , a subsidiary of the Arkema Group and a global player in specialty adhesives for the construction, consumer and industrial markets, develops innovative and multifunctional sealing and bonding solutions that have been shaping our daily lives for over 130 years .
 Role Description The R&D Chemist PU Foam role is a full-time on-site position based in Buftea. The role involves developing and optimizing polyurethane foam formulations, conducting laboratory experiments, and analyzing test results to improve product performance, safety, and sustainability. 
 Key Responsibilities: 
Developing, optimizing, and improving products and technologies within our PU foam portfolio;
Identifying trends, variations, and correlations between formulation parameters, process conditions, and product performance
Executing necessary physical and chemical tests and analyses; 
Using Microsoft Excel for data organization, calculations, comparative analyses, charts, statistics, and technical reports
Close cooperation with cross-functional teams, including production, and quality control laboratory;
Maintain contacts with customers and suppliers;
Convert customer needs into production and application capabilities;
 Qualifications 
University degree – degree in chemistry;
Experience in research and development, minimum of 2 years;
English language skills, both verbal and in writing;
Good knowledge of MS Office;
Detail oriented;
Ability to plan, organize and control a process;
Excellent interpersonal and communications abilities;
Statistical analysis is a plus;
